WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:08.019 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  over the last few days i've been playing  through the new rainbow six extraction  i'll be the first to admit that leading  up to this point i wasn't overly excited  by what i'd seen  but after around 20 hours of game time  i'm struggling to put it down  in this video i'll be running through  some of the mechanics and activities and  give some of my thoughts around what it  does well and what could be improved on  rainbow six extraction doesn't have a  campaign as such it's more of a  progression system where you would jump  in run one to three objective based  missions and extract  if successful you earn experience and  gear and start unlocking new map  locations and more challenging content  and modes  there is no linear mission line to  follow  once unlocked there is four locations  within each of these there are three  sectors you can pick from  you will then be shown a group of three  random objectives for each sub-zone of  the operation  once you've chosen your operator you and  your team are dropped into the first  subzone  if you're anything like me and you've  been playing too many run and gun  shooters for a while you'll find this a  little challenging to start with on my  very first mission i ran solo guns are  blazing and i think i was dead in about  three minutes  the objectives vary quite considerably  and for maximum success each of these  should be tackled in different ways  the majority of the time stealth is your  friend though for some of the more  challenging objectives it's a given that  you'll end up an open gunfight  eventually  however there are some we may not need  to fire your weapon at all  the maps are much larger than i was  expecting probably two to three times  the size of a typical siege map  the enemies are crazy  my first encounter with them when  playing solo late at night they scare  the crap out of me  they're fast loud and you can hear their  creepy noises when you start getting  close  there are more than 10 different types  of enemy to kill each with their own  abilities and behaviors these range from  your typical zombie-like grunts to the  behemoth smashes  there are also a number of different  alien things dotted around certain maps  like spores sludge squishy blobby things  that drop down from the ceiling and  attach to you but there is also a chance  for certain mutations to appear this  could lead to some enemies gaining a  cloaking ability or having a hardened  shell plus a number of others so i  haven't come across yet  each enemy has a weak spot or a best way  of taking it down so you have to be  careful with how you approach each fight  again coordination is key  sometimes you'll even need someone to be  the bait  while it's possible to solo play it is  considerably more difficult  with a bit of practice and a lot of  mucking around with my operator loadouts  i'm now able to complete a set of three  objectives on my own but i think the  scaling for solo play could be tweaked a  bit  as i said it's still completely possible  just more challenging with certain  objectives and much slower  i'm traditionally more of a solo player  but i personally found it a more  enjoyable tactical experience with a  team  especially when you start synchronizing  your operators and strategies  there is matchmaking but given the  coordination required i can see that  being a little bit hit and miss  depending on who you end up being  matched with  the operators have been taken directly  from rainbow six siege they've been  somewhat tweaked to match the different  style of gameplay but still feel very  much the same  one of the things i like most is the  fact that the operator damage and deaths  carry over  i don't just mean while progressing  through the different types of  objectives while on mission but after  each mission is finished as well  it makes it properly feel like you're  running with a roster  if you have a favorite operator you  can't just keep using it over and over  even on the best runs you're likely to  take a bit of damage  yes you can be healed by various things  while on missions but this is just  temporary  in order to bring your operator back to  full health you need to let them rest  while using other operators the  experience they gained has a direct  effect on how much health they will  receive the more experience gained the  more health that is given to your  injured operators  again this is just another area where  solo player is a little bit tougher you  generally take a little more damage and  experience takes a little longer to gain  it is possible to use an operator who  isn't at full health but depending on  how much damage you'd be making things  hard for yourself  however there is a limit if too injured  you'll need to wait until they've healed  a bit before you can use them again if  your operator is fully downed while out  on a mission and one of your teammates  was unable to carry you back and extract  your operator becomes mia  before you are able to heal and use this  operator again it needs to be  rescued all in all i quite like this  feature as it has you thinking a bit  more around which operator to use and it  also further adds to the tactical nature  of how you choose to play the missions  as taking some massive damage can  essentially remove the operator from the  roster while it heals  there are two things you are levelling  your operators and your personal  milestone  as you'd expect you level up your  operators by using them on missions  all experience gained will go through to  your milestone level as well  gaining experience with your operators  will open up new weapons and gear as  well as increasing certain base stats  like armor and speed  this will also unlock upgrades to the  gadget in some cases making them  considerably more effective  milestone levels will unlock more  operators and mission locations as well  as the in-game content  on top of this more gear and tech will  become available over time allowing more  options for your operator loadouts  another way to gain a bit of experience  is through the challenges  each location has a list of challenges  to complete they get progressively more  difficult  these will reward you with experience a  piece of the law and the occasional  cosmetic item  the story direction of extraction is a  little weird for a tom clancy game  but after the outbreak event the  community pushed for them to make a mode  or game based on this so we can hardly  complain about them listening to the  player base  but it would be nice if they'd taken the  story in a different direction  say if the aliens were replaced with a  terrorist organization or something but  it is what it is  one thing i really must note is that the  build felt very clean i didn't have any  technical issues at all this is a very  positive sign though we'll see how the  servers handled the increased load after  release  unfortunately i didn't give far enough  by the time of writing this to try out  the in-game activities  but these include limited time crisis  events where game-changing perimeters  are added as well as introducing new  enemies  weekly assignments that will offer  gameplay modifiers like veteran mode  which removes the hud gives you limited  ammo and enables friendly fire  and the maelstrom protocol where you are  challenged to run through nine sub-zones  each increasing in difficulty  this activity is ranked top schools will  earn react credits and unique headgear  all in all i went from being skeptical  to addicted within only a few hours  i do have concerns about the  replayability once i've levelled up my  favorite operators and have reached the  level 30 milestone  from what i've seen of the in-game so  far it doesn't really seem that  compelling to me but as i said i haven't  played it yet so hopefully i'm proven  wrong  this has been one of the most enjoyable  true tactical pve shooters that have  played in a long time  if you're interested in this style of  game i definitely recommend it  but in its current state you'll have a  better time playing with a couple of  friends  it just doesn't really feel like it's  been completely optimized for solo play  yet  fortunately they've included the buddy  pass system where you can invite two  people to play for free for up to two  weeks and there is cross play so it  makes it a little easier to bring  friends on board  anyway hopefully you found this useful  and i'll catch in the next one cheers  [Applause]  [Music]

